[# promotional/sale-badge: a big round or square SALE / percentage badge, for placing beside or above an offer.

   A fixed-size table cell with a background color. The circle needs border-radius, which Outlook desktop ignores, so
   it renders as a square there with the same text.

   Compatibility
   - Outlook desktop: size, color and text are honored, the circle becomes a square.
   - Gmail apps: fine.
   - Dark mode: the badge keeps its own colors. #]
<mj-text[[ cc(cls) ]] align="[[ s.align ]]" padding="[[ s.padding ]]">
  <table role="presentation" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" align="[[ s.align ]]" style="display:inline-table;"><tr>
    <td align="center" valign="middle" width="[[ s.size ]]" height="[[ s.size ]]" bgcolor="[[ s.background ]]" style="width:[[ s.size ]];height:[[ s.size ]];border-radius:[[ s.radius ]];background:[[ s.background ]];color:[[ s.color ]];font-family:[[ t.fonts.heading ]];font-weight:bold;">
      <div style="font-size:[[ s.textSize ]];line-height:1.1;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;">[[ data.text ]]</div>
      [% if data.sub %]<div style="font-size:11px;line-height:1.2;padding-top:2px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;">[[ data.sub ]]</div>[% endif %]
    </td>
  </tr></table>
</mj-text>
